A table with AUTOINCREMENT is renamed in case alone (`Dish` to `dish`), the
same name to SQLite: rebuilt, and its counter carried under the new spelling.

== before
CREATE TABLE Dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO Dish (name) VALUES ('soup'), ('bread');
DELETE FROM Dish WHERE name = 'bread';

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 5 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "Dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_Dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `dish`: AUTOINCREMENT goes on from where it was
    INSERT INTO sqlite_sequence (name, seq) SELECT 'dish', seq FROM sqlite_sequence WHERE name = 'roux_old_Dish'
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, name
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "name") SELECT "id", "name" FROM "roux_old_Dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_Dish"
